@page "/drawer"

<PageTitle>Drawer · Bheadless</PageTitle>

<div class="bb-intro">
    <h1>Drawer</h1>
    <p class="bb-subtitle">A modal dialog that slides in from an edge of the screen - a bottom sheet, a side panel - and can be swiped away.</p>
</div>

<SectionSwitcher Slug="drawer" />

<DemoBlock Title="Bottom sheet" Code="@_sheetCode" Css="@_css">
    <Description>
        A drawer is a dialog: <code>role="dialog"</code> named by <code>BitBhDrawerTitle</code> and described by
        <code>BitBhDrawerDescription</code>, focus trapped inside and returned to the trigger, the page behind it
        <code>inert</code> with its scroll locked, Escape and the backdrop close it. Drag the sheet down - anywhere, or by its
        <code>BitBhDrawerHandle</code> - and it follows the pointer through <code>--bit-bh-drawer-swipe-movement-y</code>
        (the backdrop fades with <code>--bit-bh-drawer-swipe-progress</code>); let go past <code>SwipeThreshold</code> (a quarter of
        its height) or flick it, and it closes, otherwise it settles back. A drag in the list while it is scrolled away from its top
        scrolls the list instead.
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <BitBhDrawer>
            <BitBhDrawerTrigger class="btn">Open sheet</BitBhDrawerTrigger>
            <BitBhDrawerBackdrop class="drawer-backdrop" />
            <BitBhDrawerPanel class="drawer-panel">
                <BitBhDrawerHandle class="drawer-handle" />
                <BitBhDrawerTitle class="drawer-title">Recent activity</BitBhDrawerTitle>
                <BitBhDrawerDescription class="drawer-description">Swipe down or press Escape to close.</BitBhDrawerDescription>
                <ul class="drawer-body">
                    @for (var i = 1; i <= 20; i++)
                    {
                        <li>Event @i</li>
                    }
                </ul>
                <div class="drawer-actions">
                    <BitBhDrawerClose class="btn btn-primary">Done</BitBhDrawerClose>
                </div>
            </BitBhDrawerPanel>
        </BitBhDrawer>
    </LiveContent>
</DemoBlock>

<DemoBlock Title="Sides" Code="@_sidesCode" Css="@_css">
    <Description>
        <code>Side</code> attaches the drawer to any edge; <code>Start</code> and <code>End</code> follow the reading direction
        (<code>Start</code> is the right edge in right-to-left). Every part gets <code>data-side</code>, and a swipe towards that edge
        moves the panel along <code>--bit-bh-drawer-swipe-movement-x</code>. Bound with <code>@@bind-Open</code>, the drawer needs no
        trigger of its own: focus returns to the button that opened it.
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <div class="demo-row">
            <button type="button" class="btn" @onclick="() => OpenSide(BitBhDrawerSide.Start)">Start</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" @onclick="() => OpenSide(BitBhDrawerSide.End)">End</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" @onclick="() => OpenSide(BitBhDrawerSide.Top)">Top</button>
        </div>
        <BitBhDrawer @bind-Open="sideOpen" Side="side">
            <BitBhDrawerBackdrop class="drawer-backdrop" />
            <BitBhDrawerPanel class="drawer-panel">
                <BitBhDrawerTitle class="drawer-title">Navigation</BitBhDrawerTitle>
                <nav class="drawer-nav" aria-label="Drawer example">
                    <a href="drawer#home" @onclick="() => sideOpen = false">Home</a>
                    <a href="drawer#projects" @onclick="() => sideOpen = false">Projects</a>
                    <a href="drawer#settings" @onclick="() => sideOpen = false">Settings</a>
                </nav>
                <div class="drawer-actions">
                    <BitBhDrawerClose class="btn">Close</BitBhDrawerClose>
                </div>
            </BitBhDrawerPanel>
        </BitBhDrawer>
    </LiveContent>
</DemoBlock>

<DemoBlock Title="Nested drawers" Code="@_nestedCode" Css="@_css">
    <Description>
        A drawer opened from another drawer's panel gets <code>data-nested</code>; the one behind it gets
        <code>data-nested-drawer-open</code> and <code>--bit-bh-nested-drawers</code> (how many are open in front of it), here used to
        scale it back. Closing the outer drawer closes the inner one too. <code>OnDismissRequest</code> sees every Escape, outside
        press and swipe (<code>BitBhDismissReason.Swipe</code>) and can cancel it.
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <BitBhDrawer OnDismissRequest="r => lastReason = r.Reason">
            <BitBhDrawerTrigger class="btn">Open settings</BitBhDrawerTrigger>
            <BitBhDrawerBackdrop class="drawer-backdrop" />
            <BitBhDrawerPanel class="drawer-panel">
                <BitBhDrawerHandle class="drawer-handle" />
                <BitBhDrawerTitle class="drawer-title">Settings</BitBhDrawerTitle>
                <BitBhDrawerDescription class="drawer-description">Some settings open a drawer of their own.</BitBhDrawerDescription>
                <BitBhDrawer>
                    <BitBhDrawerTrigger class="btn">Advanced…</BitBhDrawerTrigger>
                    <BitBhDrawerBackdrop class="drawer-backdrop" />
                    <BitBhDrawerPanel class="drawer-panel">
                        <BitBhDrawerHandle class="drawer-handle" />
                        <BitBhDrawerTitle class="drawer-title">Advanced settings</BitBhDrawerTitle>
                        <BitBhDrawerDescription class="drawer-description">The settings drawer steps back behind this one.</BitBhDrawerDescription>
                        <div class="drawer-actions">
                            <BitBhDrawerClose class="btn btn-primary">Done</BitBhDrawerClose>
                        </div>
                    </BitBhDrawerPanel>
                </BitBhDrawer>
                <div class="drawer-actions">
                    <BitBhDrawerClose class="btn">Close</BitBhDrawerClose>
                </div>
            </BitBhDrawerPanel>
        </BitBhDrawer>
        <span class="demo-output">Last dismissed by: <strong>@(lastReason?.ToString() ?? "nothing yet")</strong></span>
    </LiveContent>
</DemoBlock>

<DemoBlock Title="Snap points" Code="@_snapCode" Css="@_css">
    <Description>
        <code>SnapPoints</code> let the drawer rest part open - here a 160px peek, half the screen and all of it (Vaul-style
        fractions of the viewport, or pixels). Drag it and it settles on the nearest one; flick it and it moves on to the next; drag
        it below the smallest and it closes. The runtime rests the panel through <code>--bit-bh-drawer-snap-point-offset-y</code>
        (<code>-x</code> for a side panel), added to the swipe movement, and every part gets <code>data-snap-point</code>, which
        <code>@@bind-ActiveSnapPoint</code> follows. Without a pointer, the <code>BitBhDrawerHandle</code> is a slider - arrow
        keys, Home / End, Enter to cycle - and Tab into the part of the panel a snap point hides opens it far enough to show it.
    </Description>
    <LiveContent>
        <div class="demo-row">
            <button type="button" class="btn" @onclick="() => OpenSnap(BitBhDrawerSide.Bottom)">Bottom sheet</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" @onclick="() => OpenSnap(BitBhDrawerSide.End)">Side panel</button>
        </div>
        <BitBhDrawer @bind-Open="snapOpen" Side="snapSide" SnapPoints="SnapPointsFor(snapSide)" @bind-ActiveSnapPoint="snapPoint">
            <BitBhDrawerBackdrop class="drawer-backdrop drawer-backdrop-snap" />
            <BitBhDrawerPanel class="drawer-panel drawer-panel-snap">
                <BitBhDrawerHandle class="drawer-handle" />
                <BitBhDrawerTitle class="drawer-title">Trip details</BitBhDrawerTitle>
                <BitBhDrawerDescription class="drawer-description">Drag or flick the handle, or focus it and use the arrow keys.</BitBhDrawerDescription>
                <ul class="drawer-body" tabindex="0" aria-label="Stops">
                    @for (var i = 1; i <= 12; i++)
                    {
                        <li>Stop @i</li>
                    }
                </ul>
                <div class="drawer-actions">
                    <BitBhDrawerClose class="btn btn-primary">Done</BitBhDrawerClose>
                </div>
            </BitBhDrawerPanel>
        </BitBhDrawer>
        <span class="demo-output">Snap point: <strong>@(snapPoint?.ToString() ?? "none")</strong></span>
    </LiveContent>
</DemoBlock>

